{"name":"Cotton Muslin","hex":"#eed09c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cotton","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fibrous substance:\n A soft, fibrous, usually white substance consisting of fine hairs, especially the substance around the seeds of a plant of genus Gossypium.\n Any similar soft, fibrous, white substance of fine hairs, of any origin.","A soft, fibrous, usually white substance consisting of fine hairs, especially the substance around the seeds of a plant of genus Gossypium."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of cotton."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cotton"},{"term":"muslin","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several varieties of thin cotton cloth.","Fabric made of cotton, flax (linen), hemp, or silk, finely or coarsely woven."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/muslin"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cotton","blocks":[{"text":"Cotton is a soft, fluffy staple fiber that grows in a boll, or protective case, around the seeds of the cotton plants of the genus Gossypium in the mallow family Malvaceae. The fiber is almost pure cellulose and may contain minor percentages of waxes, fats, pectins, and water. Under natural conditions, cotton bolls facilitate the dispersal of the seeds."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/CottonPlant.JPG/330px-CottonPlant.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cotton","wikidata":"Q11457"},{"title":"Muslin","blocks":[{"text":"Muslin is a cotton fabric of plain weave. It is made in a wide range of weights from delicate sheers to coarse sheeting."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Woman%27s_muslin_dress_c._1855.jpg/330px-Woman%27s_muslin_dress_c._1855.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muslin","wikidata":"Q725457"}],"images":[{"srcse